# Image TODO: hami-scheduler-webhook-v1.png

## Purpose
Show that one HAMi pod carries two containers (scheduler + webhook = 2/2) and which
chart objects accompany it, with the device-plugin DaemonSet clearly disabled.

## Composition breakdown
- Center: a pod card "hami-scheduler  2/2" split into two container boxes.
  - Top box "scheduler" → arrow to Kubernetes API server, labeled "binds GPU pods to
    nodes".
  - Bottom box "webhook" → arrow from an incoming pod, labeled "mutates
    spec.schedulerName".
- Below the pod: four small resource cards — Deployment, Service, ConfigMap,
  ServiceAccount.
- Off to the side: a greyed-out, dashed card "device-plugin DaemonSet — DISABLED"
  with a red X.

## Gemini prompt
Create a flat technical diagram of the HAMi scheduler pod in the kube-system
namespace. Draw one pod card labeled "hami-scheduler  2/2" split into two stacked
container boxes. From the top box labeled "scheduler", draw an arrow to a Kubernetes
API server box labeled "binds GPU pods to nodes". Into the bottom box labeled
"webhook", draw an arrow from an incoming pod labeled "mutates spec.schedulerName".
Below the pod, draw four small rounded resource cards labeled "Deployment",
"Service", "ConfigMap", and "ServiceAccount". Off to the right, draw a greyed-out,
dashed-border card labeled "device-plugin DaemonSet — DISABLED" with a small red X.
Style: flat technical illustration, dark navy background (#0D1117), electric blue
(#2F81F7) and neon green (#39D353) accents, off-white (#E6EDF3) labels, subtle
hexagonal grid texture at 10% opacity, no photorealism, no gradients on solid
elements, clean sans-serif labels, developer education platform aesthetic.
Aspect ratio 16:9.
